# Who must review a change to what the checks on `main` decide.
#
# A pull request runs its own copy of every workflow it changes, in the merge
# queue as on its own run, and the actions, scripts, hooks and configuration
# those workflows run come from the same checkout. So a change to any of them
# can change what a required check decides, including a check on that same
# pull request. `main`'s ruleset requires a code owner's review; these entries
# are what give that rule something to apply to.
#
# An entry is an anchored path or directory, or a file name that matches at
# any depth; the last entry that matches a path decides its owners, as GitHub
# reads this file.
# `scripts/merge-queue-workflows.test.mjs` holds each required check's
# workflow, and everything it runs, to having an owner here.

# The workflows, their actions and this file.
/.github/                    @mobeenabdullah

# The hooks, and the repository's scripts.
/.husky/                     @mobeenabdullah
/scripts/                    @mobeenabdullah
/pnpm-workspace.yaml         @mobeenabdullah

# Every manifest, test configuration and task graph, wherever it sits: a CI
# lane runs the test script a manifest names, with the configuration beside
# it, over the task graph Turbo reads. A no-op test script would pass its lane.
package.json                 @mobeenabdullah
vitest*.config.*             @mobeenabdullah
playwright*.config.*         @mobeenabdullah
turbo.json                   @mobeenabdullah
turbo.jsonc                  @mobeenabdullah

# The configuration the checks read.
/.changeset/config.json      @mobeenabdullah
/.commitlintrc.json          @mobeenabdullah
/.fallowrc.jsonc             @mobeenabdullah
/.gitleaks.toml              @mobeenabdullah
/eslint.config.mjs           @mobeenabdullah
/eslint.scripts.config.mjs   @mobeenabdullah
/fallow-health-baseline.json @mobeenabdullah
/lint-staged.config.mjs      @mobeenabdullah
/tsconfig.base.json          @mobeenabdullah
